### Scope of record — mandatory two-predicate split

#### A. Mathematical absorption/supply set

The note’s boxed governing claim is:

> \[
> \boxed{
> {\rm GENTOW2\!-\!B''},\qquad
> {\rm HETOW\!-\!4(c)}\text{ with its routing block},\qquad
> [{\rm GENTOW5\!-\!W}(i)].
> }
> \tag{T3-A0}
> \]

Its ledger states:

> “The absorption count is three source conclusions, not four. GENTOW-6.4 does not increment it.”

Thus the mathematical absorption set has exactly three source conclusions: ABS-G2, ABS-HE4 with routing, and ABS-G5W.

#### B. Consumption/append-protocol scope

The post-acceptance record states, without truncation:

> “The three-leg checks (gpt-5.6-sol high, runs/comp5/T3CC_output.log):
> GENTOW2-B″ PASS, HETOW-4 PASS; GENTOW-6.4 confirmed NOT ABSORBED —
> in exact agreement with this note's own (G6-NONINSTANCE) display.
> The unit's scope of record is therefore TWO absorptions + one
> documented non-instance; GENTOW-6.4 retains its own certified proof
> (the blueprint's third target was honestly narrowed at revision).
> The absorbed notes' dated "absorbed by S-2 as instance" appends may
> now land for the two passing absorptions.”

The blueprint’s ordered target triple is GENTOW2-B″, HETOW-4, GENTOW-6.4. Accordingly, its third target is GENTOW-6.4. The protocol checked those three targets, absorbed the first two, and retained the third as a non-instance.

ABS-G5W is the **FOURTH protocol-relevant source item**, added by the revised note outside the blueprint target triple. Its status is:

> **ABSORBED per T3-A0 and §7; consumption check + append outstanding.**

This does not change the mathematical absorption count of three.

